cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this reproducibility pack, please cite the working paper."
title: "Global Weakness, Local Strength — Reproducibility Pack"
authors:
  - family-names: Jin
    given-names: Huannian
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-20"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/nemo02070118/boatfx-repro"
abstract: >-
  Public reproducibility surface for Global Weakness, Local Strength:
  the blind spot of unconditional factor screening, and its companion working
  paper The Resolution Limit of Factor Discovery: Why the Replication Crisis
  Is a Measurement Problem (q^2 = tau/(1+tau), half-recovery at m* approximately
  1.3 factors). Ships factor language, a 60-factor sample,
  and headline tilt outputs so deployable economics can be regenerated
  without proprietary router source.
keywords:
  - factor investing
  - regime
  - reproducibility
  - unconditional screening
  - machine-generated factors
preferred-citation:
  type: unpublished
  title: "Global Weakness, Local Strength: The Blind Spot of Unconditional Factor Screening"
  authors:
    - family-names: Jin
      given-names: Huannian
  year: 2026
  notes: "Journal of Finance MS 2026-0738: passed desk review, in external review (editor in charge: Antoinette Schoar); submitted to Eastern Finance Association (EFA). Companion working paper: The Resolution Limit of Factor Discovery — Why the Replication Crisis Is a Measurement Problem (Oct 2026 draft; repro at github.com/nemo02070118/localstrength-repro; acceptance not claimed)."
